<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  network_security_config.xml — the one address a debug build may reach in the clear.

  History
    2026-08-09  A. Sigdel  Created with #513.

  This file lives in src/debug and has no counterpart in src/main, which is the
  whole of its design. A release build has no network security config at all, so
  it inherits the platform default and cannot send cleartext anywhere — including
  to the address below. Nothing here can ship.

  10.0.2.2 is the emulator's alias for the host loopback. It is the only way a
  stub model server running on a developer's machine is reachable from the
  application under test, and #513 argues why that server has to exist: without
  it the tool loop can only be exercised by paying a third party, so the most
  interesting part of this application has no test a person can run.

  Scoped to that one address rather than cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" on the
  base config. The broad form would also permit a plain-HTTP model endpoint on a
  real network, which is a request carrying a conversation and everything the
  agent read off the screen.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">10.0.2.2</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
